imbridge caller-chosen GUIDs: send-message, send-multipart, send-attachment and classic tapbacks take an optional
"guid" (a UUID) and create the message with it instead of letting IMCore pick one, so a caller that recorded the GUID
before sending can find exactly that message in chat.db after a timeout or a crash. Anything that isn't a UUID is
ignored. (Emoji tapbacks go through a factory with no GUID, and keep IMCore's.)

diff --git a/Messages/MacOS-11+/BlueBubblesHelper/BlueBubblesHelper.m b/Messages/MacOS-11+/BlueBubblesHelper/BlueBubblesHelper.m
index a7ab088..e0e6c9f 100644
